            <ArticleTitle>[Ureteropelvic junction obstruction with renal hypertension].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>190-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1055/s-0031-1271420</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Renal hypertension can occur with unilateral ureteropelvic junction obstruction and consecutive hydronephrosis. It is rarely the main symptom, normally in adults flank pain is in the foreground. We report a case of renal hypertension with ureteropelvic junction obstruction successfully corrected by laparoscopic pyeloplasty and discuss the pathophysiology.</AbstractText>
